  "body": "This spec chunk...\n https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#the-webkit-text-stroke\n...says this property accepts: `<line-width> || [ currentcolor | <color> ]`\n\nI think this should just be simplified to`<line-width> || <color>`\n\nWe don't need `currentcolor |` there -- it's already implied by `<color>`. Specifically, the css-color-3 spec says: \n\n> CSS3 extends the color value to include the ‘currentColor’ keyword to allow its use with all properties that accept a <color> value. This simplifies the definition of those properties in CSS3.\n",
